      "plaintextBody": "Victor Juarez \u003cvictor.juarez@optconnect.com\u003e mentioned you in Net-Eng while\nyou were away\n\nTyson Goulding\n\nTyson Goulding\n\nzabbix report was disabled, but it did see the problem on teal tunnel This\nwas on me testing to pagerduty @Andy Cutright\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nI have what I believe is the original Webbing engineering configuration in\nthe Machine_configuration repository. I am thinking about adding it to\nhttps://optconnect.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/NH/pages/270925825/NETWORK+DOCUMENTATION\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nor do we want somewhere else to track engineering documentation?\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nhey folks i've added a link from the Net-Eng Confluence Wiki to the the UT\nNETWORK-HOME Confluence Wiki\nhttps://optconnect.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/NetEng/overview\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nthis should help us navigate from \"our\" team wiki to the UT wiki as\nnecessary\n\nJacob Katutu\n\nJacob Katutu\n\n@Victor Juarez I made some changes to the new router.. adding the snmp so\nwe can start monitoring it while working on it today\n\nScreenshot 2026-08-25 at 10.57.12 AM.png\n\nJacob Katutu\n\nJacob Katutu\n\n@Tyson Goulding I moved the Carrier-HA meeting to 11:30, incase you are\nwondering\n\nVictor Juarez\n\nVictor Juarez\n\n@Tyson Goulding Hi Tyson, Jacob and I have finished configuring the new\nCarrier HA Router 2 (VZW), including the reordered policies, updated\ntransform sets, and ACLs. To prevent production impact, we have kept the\ngigabit 1 interface and tunnels 0/1 shut down. We are ready to validate\nconnectivity via pinging the tunnels and would like to coordinate a time to\ntest this, ideally outside of production hours. Please let us know what\nworks for you.\n\nJacob Katutu\n\nJacob Katutu\n\nLunch\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nAndy Cutright\n\nOut for a bit\n\nOpen in Google Chat\n\nUpdate your notification preferences\n\nYou can keep receiving email notifications for all missed messages, and\nalso adjust each conversation's individual notification preferences.\n\nLearn about notifications\n\nGoogle Chat: An intelligent messaging app, built for teams.\nGoogle LLC, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA\nYou have received this email because you have been mentioned in this\nconversation by a Google Chat user. You cannot reply to this email.\nUnsubscribe from these emails by changing your email reminder preferences\nfor Google Chat. Email reminder preferences cannot be set on mobile\ndevices. Learn more\nLogo for Google",
